<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Bu Said dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Al Said, Busaidi dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Al Bu Said dynasty has ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> since the 1740s, when Ahmad ibn Said expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> and was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> in place of the Ya'aruba. Its sultans built a maritime empire from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> and Zanzibar over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> coast; after 1856 the family split into separate Omani and Zanzibari lines, the latter overthrown in 1964.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-bu-said-dynasty.jpg" alt="Al Bu Said dynasty" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Standard_of_Oman.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
